alls back to the default \"DropZone\" label provided by React Aria."],[1069,"**`ButtonGroup`** — a cluster of related actions, typically inside a `Footer` (an end-aligned, wrapping row with `role=\"group\"`)."],[1066,"**`Content`** — the primary body region (a `<section>`, a column that grows to fill)."],[366,"**`Field`** — stacks a field's label, control, description, and error in one consistently spaced column (pure layout — a `Flex` column with the standard field gap)."],[371,"**`FieldButton`** — an actionable control placed inside the box, such as the NumberField steppers or a search submit (a click target within the group)."],[373,"**`FieldDescription`** — helper text that explains the field; renders nothing when empty (wraps the antares `Text` with `slot=\"description\"`)."],[374,"**`FieldError`** — surfaces the field's validation messages when it is invalid, and nothing when valid (a thin wrapper over React Aria `FieldError`)."],[368,"**`FieldGroup`** — the bordered box that visually unites a field's controls and reflects their shared focus, disabled, and invalid state. Used only by \"boxed\" fields (TextField, NumberField, Select, DateField); presentationally it is a React Aria `Group`."],[369,"**`FieldInput`** — the single-line control the user types into (a normalized React Aria `Input` given antares spacing via `Box`)."],[367,"**`FieldLabel`** — names the field and flags whether it's required (wraps React Aria `Label`, rendering an optional `*` indicator)."],[370,"**`FieldTextArea`** — the multiline control the user types into (a normalized React Aria `TextArea` given antares spacing via `Box`)."],[372,"**`FieldTrigger`** — a full-width value-display button inside the box that opens an overlay (used by Select and DatePicker): a value area plus a trailing icon, laid out across the group. `variant=\"select\"` is transparent and input-like; `variant=\"control\"` is a filled segment inside a shared group."],[1068,"**`Footer`** — the bottom region: secondary content and/or actions (a `<footer>` row that spaces its contents apart)."],[1067,"**`Header`** — the top region: title area and optional trailing close (a `<header>` row that spaces its contents apart)."],[471,"**`icon.content`**: Overrides the BentoIllustration component - affects SVG transformations (rotate, flip), accessibility attributes (`role`, `focusable`, `aria-labelledby`), viewBox calculations, and final SVG element rendering"],[470,"**`icon`**: Overrides the entire BentoIcon component - affects icon loading, caching, sprite/SVG mode switching, data attributes, and the overall icon wrapper"],[478,"**`ondemand(loader)`**: Register an asynchronous icon loader (returns unregister function)"],[479,"**`parser(svgString)`**: Parse SVG strings into React elements"],[477,"**`set(icons)`**: Synchronously add icons to the store"],[1351,"**`size` is the tier.** The eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`, and\nthe body on `body`, so there is no table to memorize."],[845,"**A step isn't clickable:** it has no `onPress`, so it's inert by design. Add `onPress` to make it interactive."],[458,"**Accessibility ready**: Built-in support for screen readers and keyboard navigation"],[1428,"**Accessibility ready**: Keyboard navigation, screen reader support, and semantic HTML"],[463,"**Accessibility**: `aria-label`, `aria-describedby`, `role`, `title`"],[1072,"**Adopted** — placed inside a parent that provides its context (`ContentContext`, `HeaderContext`, `FooterContext`, `ButtonGroupContext`), it picks up that parent's styling and spacing automatically. Merge precedence is defaults \\< parent context \\< consumer props (`className` concatenates, handlers chain), via React Aria's `useContextProps`."],[1228,"**Adornments**: Optional `leadingText` and `trailingText` for fixed text before or after the input (e.g. `$`, `.00`, `px`)"],[1349,"**An explicit prop on a child always wins** over what the lockup supplies. Pass\n`<Tag slot=\"eyebrow\" size=\"sm\">` 